    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "The polynomial $P(x)=x^3+6x^2+9x+p$ is tangent to the $x$-axis at a point. Find the values of $p$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$p=0$ or $p=4$.",
      "worked": "At a point of tangency to the $x$-axis, $P(x)=0$ and $P'(x)=0$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}P'(x)&=3x^2+12x+9\\\\P'(x)&=3(x+1)(x+3).\\end{aligned}$$\nThus $P'(x)=0$ at $x=-3$ or $x=-1$.\nFor $x=-3$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(-3)&=-27+54-27+p\\\\P(-3)&=p\\\\p&=0.\\end{aligned}$$\nFor $x=-1$,\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(-1)&=-1+6-9+p\\\\P(-1)&=p-4\\\\p&=4.\\end{aligned}$$\nHence $p=0$ or $p=4$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 43
  },
